  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>lake-child - the child: lands each batch of pdi-signups records in the
lake, one Avro file per batch, exactly as they arrived.

1. Get records from stream: key, message, topic, partition, offset, timestamp.
2. Get system info: landed_at, system date (fixed): one time for the batch.
3. Select values: topic, partition, offset, timestamp renamed kafka_topic,
   kafka_partition, kafka_offset, kafka_timestamp; message; landed_at.
4. Land in the lake (Avro output): pvfs://MinIO/streaming-lake/signups_ and
   the date and time, yyyyMMdd_HHmmss_SSS'.avro', so signups_&lt;time&gt;.avro; Deflate,
   schema embedded: record signup_event, namespace com.acme.lake.

Needs the VFS connection MinIO and the bucket streaming-lake.</note>
      <xloc>32</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>520</width>
      <heigth>230</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
